  "description": "The strict profile of kubectl-readonly: the same read-only policy (writes,\nexec and secret values blocked), and kubectl runs without\nKUBECTL_EXTERNAL_DIFF (runs a program on kubectl diff) and with kuberc\ndisabled (KUBERC=off).\nOther variables pass through, so credential plugins and proxies work.\n\nDesigned to guard against human errors and AI assistants overstepping their\ninstructions. Does NOT protect against deliberate bypass attempts.\n",
